From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:45:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] Round 6: Interleave independent catchment candidates

Groups of up to four untraced catchment candidates now advance
together over the shared forcing in widths 4, 2 and 1 under the same
unmonitored-budget condition as the reservoir kernel. Scalar and lane
paths share catchment_day and score_day, so each candidate performs
the same floating-point operations in the same order and results are
bit-identical; logical steps are unchanged. A new test compares grouped
and guarded single-candidate runs across exponents, invalid rows, snow
and dry spells.

Workload: domain (48 full catchment records of 2,400 days), 11 samples
against round 5.
Before median: 2.726 ms. After median: 1.168 ms. Speedup: 2.33x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
